steps.text:
The route is a careful history, then ruling out other causes [[c:ot-history]]. The consensus lists:

- organic disease (a physical illness) and infection;
- too little energy, carbohydrate or protein;
- iron or magnesium deficiency;
- allergies;
- and a search for the trigger.

Organic causes should be screened for when underperformance and symptoms persist despite a rest period, or at once if the history points to one [[c:ot-screen]].

This ties to the last lesson: low energy availability is on the list, because it can look exactly like OTS (see the REDs lessons).
